Pre-existing product-behavior gap (NOT introduced by NEARS-2927; add_or_update_translations()
is untouched by this ticket's diff — confirmed via
`git diff development...HEAD -- Admin/app/CentralLogics/Helpers.php | grep add_or_update_translations`
returning zero hits). Not a security defect: every value observed on every path below is fully
sanitized. Flagging because it could confuse an admin auditing "is this really neutralized" if
they don't know the visible page can lag the DB.

Mechanism:
- Item/TempProduct use HasTranslations -> TranslateScope, which eager-loads `translations`
  filtered to app()->getLocale() (default 'en') and an accessor prefers that translation's
  value over the base items.description column whenever a matching row exists.
- The vendor/admin item-edit form-write path calls Helpers::add_or_update_translations(...,
  data_value: $model->description) for the 'name'/'description' keys, which (re)writes the
  'en' translations row to match whatever was just saved to the base column.
- The bulk-import write path (Vendor/ItemController::bulk_import_data() and its Admin twin) NEVER
  calls add_or_update_translations() at all -- it writes items.description directly via
  DB::table('items')->insertGetId()/raw update, bypassing the translations table entirely.

Observed live on item 91135 (QA-2927 Primary Probe Item, store 4):
  1. Vendor form-edit set description = "Admin write probe." -> items.description AND the
     translations('en','description') row both = "Admin write probe."
  2. Admin bulk-import (Update Existing Data) then set description = "Admin bulk import test."
     -> items.description correctly updated to "Admin bulk import test." (verified via
     `SELECT description FROM items WHERE id=91135`), sanitized as expected.
  3. GET admin/pos/quick-view?product_id=91135 and admin/order/quick-view?product_id=91135
     (both TranslateScope-active reads) still rendered "Admin write probe." -- the STALE
     translations('en') row from step 1, not the true current items.description from step 2.

Impact: cosmetic/data-consistency only -- any content reaching these sinks via either path is
independently sanitized by this ticket's fix, so there is no XSS regression. Filed as a
non-blocking follow-up since it's orthogonal to NEARS-2927's scope.
